    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0419" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.731/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-23T10:00:00-03:00">May 23, 1944—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1301. Embassy’s 1299 of May 22, midnight.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d364-f1"/>
                    Following informal notification of suspension of All America’s closure Post
                    Office resolution issued early this morning modifies previous resolution
                    reported in Embassy’s 1296, of May 22<anchor n="80" xml:id="d364-f2"/> to
                    provide for strict warning to the company but no other action. It is understood
                    that issuance <pb facs="0420" n="406" xml:id="pg406"/> of second resolution
                    followed bitter quarrel within Ministry of Interior and belated realization that
                    international complications, especially as regards Mexico, might result.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
